Q1).*Maximum Score Given is a binary matrix representing a rectangular region. A balloon in a region is represented by 1 in the matrix cell, whereas an empty cell is represented by 0. Barry and his friend have a special machine that helps them in bursting the balloons such that for any balloon that is hit, all the balloons that are 4 directionally connected go on bursting. Barry and his friend play alternately and optimally, and Barry goes first. Print the maximum score Barry can achieve. Note The score implies the maximum number of balloons that the person has burst. If you hit one balloon, all the balloons that are 4 directionally connected to this balloon also burst. A similar process occurs for the rest of the balloons until there is no 4 directionally connected balloon. 4 direction implies left, right, up, and down within the matrix.(solved)
